# Keep the serverless function small: exclude the heavy engine + non-API code.
# These run on the persistent host (VPS), never on Vercel serverless.
#
# IMPORTANT: leading-slash anchors the pattern to the project root, so
# `/services/` excludes the top-level engine `backend/services/` but NOT the
# API's `backend/app/services/` (email, delayed prices) that routers import.
/jesse_custom/
/services/
/tests/
/alembic/
/alembic.ini
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.localstorage/
/requirements-engine.txt
# Tooling config only (poetry/ruff/black/pytest). Excluded so Vercel's Python
# builder uses requirements.txt instead of trying `uv lock` on a non-PEP-621
# pyproject.toml.
/pyproject.toml
